f('hmm-viterbi-sequence-map','degenerate','checked','S may be singleton but is never empty under the HMM input domain. Then the only hidden tuple is returned if every initial/emission/transition factor on it is positive; otherwise the trellis has no positive path and returns no conditional MAP.')
f('hmm-viterbi-sequence-map','endpoints','checked','The HMM trellis uses alpha_y(s)=pi(s)B(s,y_1) at the first observation and beta_y(s)=1 at the terminal layer. Thus no extra terminal factor changes the HMM joint path mass, including the T=1 frame.')
f('hmm-viterbi-sequence-map','nonempty-choice','checked','The supplied total order on S is reused on each layer, and the delegated max-product procedure takes the first maximizing predecessor and terminal state. The selected path is deterministic even when joint masses tie.')
